@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080/api

# Token del usuario demo: primero ejecutar "Login (200)" en la seccion de autenticacion
@token = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Listado (pagina 1, 8 por pagina por defecto)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies
Accept: application/json

### Busqueda por nombre y paginacion
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?search=ma&page=1&limit=5
Accept: application/json

### Detalle
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Accept: application/json

### Detalle que no existe (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/9999
Accept: application/json

### Crear (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "nombre": "Dune: Parte Dos",
  "imagen": "https://ejemplo.com/dune.jpg",
  "director": "Denis Villeneuve",
  "anio": 2024,
  "genero": "Ciencia ficcion",
  "sinopsis": "Paul Atreides se une a los Fremen."
}

### Crear con datos invalidos (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "imagen": "no-es-una-url",
  "anio": 1500
}

### Editar solo algunos campos (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "genero": "Epica"
}

### Editar limpiando un campo opcional con null (asi lo hace Ionic)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "director": null
}

### Eliminar (200)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/13
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ===================== Autenticacion =====================

### Registro (201) - cambiar el correo si ya existe
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Ana Perez",
  "email": "ana@correo.com",
  "password": "secreto123"
}

### Registro con correo repetido (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Usuario Demo",
  "email": "demo@peliculas.com",
  "password": "demo1234"
}

### Registro con datos invalidos (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "no-es-correo",
  "password": "123"
}

### Login (200) - guarda el token en la variable @token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@peliculas.com",
  "password": "demo1234"
}

### Login con contrasena incorrecta (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@peliculas.com",
  "password": "otra-clave"
}

### Usuario actual con token (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Usuario actual sin token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Crear pelicula sin token (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Sin token",
  "imagen": "https://ejemplo.com/poster.jpg"
}
